WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
Our latest wildflower is not just in charge.

2
00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:03.960
She's got a whole lot of spark

3
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.000
because she is an electrician.

4
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.550
Tanya Hicks was the first African-American woman

5
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.460
to be accepted in the Mississippi Electrical Union.

6
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.380
And the first woman accepted in her local union.

7
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.860
And Tanya is joining us now.

8
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.693
Hi, Tanya,

9
00:00:18.693 --> 00:00:20.008
(audience applauding)

10
00:00:20.008 --> 00:00:22.750
Hi.

11
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:27.610
What made you want to be an electrician?

12
00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:32.540
Yes. I was at college and I wanted to work in the Pentagon

13
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.637
and work on some sci-fi stuff and my professor said

14
00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:39.900 line:15%
the best thing I would be able to do was be a teacher,

15
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.930 line:15%
that there weren't jobs like that available for women.

16
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.890 line:15%
So that summer I was discouraged, I went

17
00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.782
and worked on a construction site

18
00:00:47.782 --> 00:00:52.633
and I saw that electricians use electricity, all day.

19
00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:58.120
And it was, I knew right then, that's what I wanted to be.

20
00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.930
I wanted to be an electrician.

21
00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:02.850
Now you started your own business.

22
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.850
And for 15 years you pretended that a man ran your company.

23
00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.783
Why did you do that?

24
00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:14.400
Well, I wanted to be taken seriously

25
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.890
and I wanted to be paid equally,

26
00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.920
and usually when people find out you're a woman

27
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.620
they want to pay you lesser.

28
00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.540 line:15%
And you don't get the same opportunity.

29
00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:27.830 line:15%
So I would go a job sites,

30
00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:29.640 line:15%
they would think I was the cleaning lady,

31
00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.080
and then when they would find out that I was a woman

32
00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.220
and I was an owner,

33
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.226
they automatically thought that I owned the company

34
00:01:37.226 --> 00:01:41.185
with my husband, and I wasn't even married.

35
00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:45.140
And so I used that as an opportunity to hide

36
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.240
so I had to build up my resume

37
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.510
and also not make being a woman

38
00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.600
or a minority my value proposition.

39
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.453
So I did that.

40
00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.490
Well, I am really excited to be your apprentice today.

41
00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.650
Will you teach me something that I did not know before?

42
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:08.000
Empower me. Pun intended.

43
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.660
Oh yes, well, today we're going to change out

44
00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:12.930 line:15%
a regular switch into a motion switch.

45
00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.460 line:15%
And Drew, you have children just like I do,

46
00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.350 line:15%
and you get tired of screaming at kids

47
00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.050 line:15%
to turn off the lights.

48
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.070 line:15%
Well, when you install a motion switch,

49
00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.056
as long as there's no activity in the room,

50
00:02:23.056 --> 00:02:24.640 line:15%
they're automatically cut off.

51
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.330 line:15%
So you ready to go?

52
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.520 line:15%
All right, teach me the ways, Tanya.

53
00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.260 line:15%
Turn me into someone I've always wanted to be,

54
00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.530
which is not the damsel in distress who calls for help,

55
00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.387
but can do it myself.

56
00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:39.470
So the first thing we're gonna do is

57
00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.827 line:15%
we're gonna make sure that the power's cut off.

58
00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.416 line:15%
All right, so here we go. Power off.

59
00:02:44.416 --> 00:02:45.249 line:15%
Got it.

60
00:02:45.249 --> 00:02:47.230 line:15%
Okay. So, next thing you're gonna do

61
00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.232 line:15%
is take your multipurpose screwdriver,

62
00:02:50.232 --> 00:02:54.300 line:15%
and, to the flathead side and take the switch off.

63
00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.640 line:15%
Turn to the left. At the same time you're doing that,

64
00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.810
I'm going to talk about the switch.

65
00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:02.930
When you take that plate off, the switch is,

66
00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.530
you'd have about three wires to it, a hot, a switch leg

67
00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:10.640
and a grounding wire.

68
00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:13.560
So the next thing that you want to do is

69
00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.560
use the same screwdriver to take out the top

70
00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.630
and the bottom screws.

71
00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.207
And then just pull it on out.

72
00:03:22.438 --> 00:03:24.683 line:15%
All right, there we go.

73
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:27.933 line:15%
All right.

74
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.070 line:15%
Okay, Drew, great job.

75
00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:34.770
Next thing you want to do is disconnect the wire.

76
00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.408
Okay, so do I wanna take the caps off?

77
00:03:37.408 --> 00:03:39.603
Yes you do, they're wire nuts.

78
00:03:39.603 --> 00:03:42.470
Those are wire nuts, you wanna take those off.

79
00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:46.580
Okay, and then I'm gonna put this in like this, okay.

80
00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.050
And then I'm gonna attach all the wires.

81
00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:51.130
Am I just going like, red wire, blue wire,

82
00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:56.130
like classic movie like, attach the wires that are matching?

83
00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.160
Yes, you're gonna take the green wire

84
00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.220
and put the green wire on the green,

85
00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:04.090 line:15%
on the wire with the green screw.

86
00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.730 line:15%
You're gonna take your black wire and connect it

87
00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.780 line:15%
with the wires coming out of the black screw.

88
00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.220
Now we've already stripped these wires for you, so.

89
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.580
And they put some pigtails on there,

90
00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:18.581
what we call it, for you.

91
00:04:18.581 --> 00:04:20.500
Pigtails, that's cute.

92
00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.471
Okay.

93
00:04:25.471 --> 00:04:27.060
Great job, you're doing great.

94
00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.070
You have to put those wires on

95
00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.513
and push it.

96
00:04:32.513 --> 00:04:35.730
Push all the wires in the box.

97
00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.040
Uh-huh.

98
00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.389 line:15%
And you see the screw at the top

99
00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:39.986 line:15%
and a screw at the bottom?

100
00:04:39.986 --> 00:04:42.153 line:15%
You're gonna put those screws on.

101
00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.953 line:15%
Yeah. Great job, yeah.

102
00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:47.213
Um.

103
00:04:47.213 --> 00:04:50.530
Yeah the entire job takes 10 to 15 minutes.

104
00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.950
So this is awesome. You're doing great.

105
00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:56.953
Yeah, yeah, so now you have that on,

106
00:04:57.987 --> 00:04:59.920 line:15%
and you can put the plate on.

107
00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.310 line:15%
Yes, that's it.

108
00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.260 line:15%
And then you want to turn the power on.

109
00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.730 line:15%
You did a great job.

110
00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.680 line:15%
All right, I'm gonna flick the power on.

111
00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:09.513
Yes.

112
00:05:09.513 --> 00:05:11.113
And then here we go, ready?

113
00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.076
Boom!

114
00:05:13.076 --> 00:05:16.920
(audience applauding)

115
00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:21.920
Tanya, if I walk by a light switch now,

116
00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:26.010
I feel like I actually know what it looks like inside.

117
00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.832
I know what to do, I know what wires to match

118
00:05:28.832 --> 00:05:32.560
and I feel like I've seen something

119
00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:35.640 line:15%
that was completely mysterious to me before

120
00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:40.040 line:15%
and I thank you for illuminating, I did it again,

121
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.980 line:15%
me into not feeling so helpless,

122
00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.680
and opening up a whole new world to me.

123
00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:46.220
Thank you.

124
00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.110
You're welcome, Drew.

125
00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.680
Well, thank you, Tanya.

126
00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.550
And we're honored to get the word out about you.

127
00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:57.080
You are such an inspiration for all the roads you are paving

128
00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.230
for everyone else.

129
00:05:58.230 --> 00:05:59.223
Thank you so much.

130
00:05:59.223 --> 00:06:01.390
You're welcome, thank you for having me.

131
00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.625
Thank you, Tanya.

132
00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:05.708
(upbeat music plays)

